Dr. Raymer -<br />
<br />
Meadowlark Elementary is an exemplary elementary school, and the Red Cross is looking for partners like you! We would love to teach your students how to serve the community through donating blood. The Red Cross Pint Size Heroes program teaches students the importance of donating blood through your school hosting a blood drive, and the students recruiting donors. All students who recruit a donor will receive a &quot;life saver&quot; medal as a thank you, and each one will be part of saving lives. We are hoping to partner with you for late spring or even talk about hosting next fall.&nbsp;I have attached a brief description of the program to give you an idea of how it works.<br />
<br />
My three children were students at Meadowlark, and I know as a parent, how many different ways students, parents, and staff are asked to give their time and money. We are commited to helping our sponsors be successful with a step-by-step process that will save lives in our community. We recently held a very successful drive at Jefferson Elementary, and we have even more tools in place now for our Pint Size Heroes to be a success!<br />
<br />
I am going to be in your area next week, and would like to stop by and and briefly discuss this opportunity for your students to save lives and learn about blood donation.&nbsp;I will only need about 15 minutes of your time, and I am happy to meet any time that is convenient for you. Please let me know when would be convenient to stop by.<br />
<br />
Thank you for your consideration!<br />
